  evidence:
    title: Names in Copper / Evidence case
    question: Which explanation fits all three signed records?
    clueNodes:
    - n22
    - n9
    - n19
    clues:
    - Repair order 17 carries the signature of a dismissed engineer.
    - The same signature appears on MOTH relay packets.
    - "The engineer\u2019s physical badge was destroyed before those packets were sent."
    answers:
    - id: accident
      title: The records disagree because of an ordinary clerical error.
      feedback: A clerical error does not explain the matching signed authorizations and their order.
      correct: 0
    - id: insider
      title: A lone outsider forged every record after the event.
      feedback: The independent receipt and earlier signatures rule out a single later forgery.
      correct: 0
    - id: rehearsal
      title: MOTH is a shared relay identity rather than one physical operator.
      feedback: A dismissed engineer still signs repair orders through the shared identity MOTH.
      correct: 1
